text:
elaine: FYI I'm onboarding the new vite-next-llamaclient starter and seeing repeated 401s on Edge; the sample's fetch helper uses sdk-edge and seems to lose auth on retry.
michael: repro steps: deploy to edge, call /api/chat -> initial 401 (token rotate) then client retries, but Authorization missing; network shows second request without header.
ravi: traced to sdk-edge retry: it rebuilds a new Request(origReq) which on some runtimes strips ephemeral headers. sdk-js keeps them intact.
docs-bot: issue 3642 filed by ravi — https://git.redwood/infra/issues/3642 labels: bug,sdk-edge
elaine: temporary sample fix: add explicit header set in helper and document under README "Edge auth note" so new devs don't get blocked.
michael: suggested helper snippet:
```js
export function safeFetch(input, init = {}, token) {
  const req = input instanceof Request ? input : new Request(input, init);
  const headers = new Headers(req.headers);
  if (token) headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
  return fetch(new Request(req.url, { method: req.method, headers, body: req.body }));
}
```
ravi: adding CI smoke under samples/e2e: run proxy that returns a 401 on first attempt and verify <=2 attempts total; will catch regressions.
elaine: also adding a one-liner to onboarding checklist for SEs: "If Edge starter hits repeated 401s, use safeFetch helper or upgrade sdk-edge."
michael: opening PR to starter repo with helper + README; will bump sdk-edge dependency once core fix merges.
elaine: thanks — follow-up: remove workaround after sdk-edge patch lands. :white_check_mark:
